    "visualLearning": {
      "type": "svg",
      "guide": "Comprehensive Visual Map of the Six Laws of Chemical Combination",
      "svgContent": "<svg viewBox='0 0 800 380' width='100%' height='auto' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' class='w-full h-auto max-w-3xl mx-auto rounded-2xl shadow-xs'>\n        <defs>\n          <linearGradient id='locGradHeader' x1='0%' y1='0%' x2='100%' y2='100%'>\n            <stop offset='0%' stop-color='#1e293b' />\n            <stop offset='100%' stop-color='#0f172a' />\n          </linearGradient>\n          <linearGradient id='locGradMass' x1='0%' y1='0%' x2='100%' y2='100%'>\n            <stop offset='0%' stop-color='#2563eb' />\n            <stop offset='100%' stop-color='#1d4ed8' />\n          </linearGradient>\n          <linearGradient id='locGradGas' x1='0%' y1='0%' x2='100%' y2='100%'>\n            <stop offset='0%' stop-color='#059669' />\n            <stop offset='100%' stop-color='#047857' />\n          </linearGradient>\n        </defs>\n\n        <rect width='800' height='380' fill='#ffffff' rx='16' class='dark:fill-slate-900'/>\n\n        <!-- Title Header -->\n        <rect x='20' y='15' width='760' height='42' rx='10' fill='url(#locGradHeader)'/>\n        <text x='400' y='41' text-anchor='middle' fill='#ffffff' font-size='14' font-weight='bold' font-family='sans-serif'>LAWS OF CHEMICAL COMBINATION — OVERVIEW</text>\n\n        <!-- Left Column: Mass & Mass Ratio Laws -->\n        <rect x='20' y='70' width='370' height='295' rx='12' fill='#f8fafc' stroke='#e2e8f0' stroke-width='1.5' class='dark:fill-slate-800/50 dark:stroke-slate-700'/>\n        <rect x='30' y='80' width='350' height='28' rx='6' fill='url(#locGradMass)'/>\n        <text x='205' y='98' text-anchor='middle' fill='#ffffff' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' font-family='sans-serif'>MASS & COMPOSITION LAWS (All Matter)</text>\n\n        <!-- Box 1: Conservation of Mass -->\n        <rect x='35' y='118' width='340' height='52' rx='8' fill='#ffffff' stroke='#cbd5e1' class='dark:fill-slate-800 dark:stroke-slate-600'/>\n        <text x='45' y='136' fill='#1e293b' font-size='11' font-weight='bold' class='dark:fill-slate-200'>1. Conservation of Mass (Lavoisier)</text>\n        <text x='45' y='153' fill='#64748b' font-size='10' class='dark:fill-slate-400'>Total Mass Reactants = Total Mass Products (m_in = m_out)</text>\n\n        <!-- Box 2: Definite Proportions -->\n        <rect x='35' y='178' width='340' height='52' rx='8' fill='#ffffff' stroke='#cbd5e1' class='dark:fill-slate-800 dark:stroke-slate-600'/>\n        <text x='45' y='196' fill='#1e293b' font-size='11' font-weight='bold' class='dark:fill-slate-200'>2. Definite Proportions (Proust)</text>\n        <text x='45' y='213' fill='#64748b' font-size='10' class='dark:fill-slate-400'>Pure compound has fixed mass ratio (e.g. H₂O → H:O = 1:8)</text>\n\n        <!-- Box 3: Multiple Proportions -->\n        <rect x='35' y='238' width='340' height='52' rx='8' fill='#ffffff' stroke='#cbd5e1' class='dark:fill-slate-800 dark:stroke-slate-600'/>\n        <text x='45' y='256' fill='#1e293b' font-size='11' font-weight='bold' class='dark:fill-slate-200'>3. Multiple Proportions (Dalton)</text>\n        <text x='45' y='273' fill='#64748b' font-size='10' class='dark:fill-slate-400'>Fixed mass of C (12g) in CO vs CO₂ → O mass ratio = 16:32 = 1:2</text>\n\n        <!-- Box 4: Reciprocal Proportions -->\n        <rect x='35' y='298' width='340' height='52' rx='8' fill='#ffffff' stroke='#cbd5e1' class='dark:fill-slate-800 dark:stroke-slate-600'/>\n        <text x='45' y='316' fill='#1e293b' font-size='11' font-weight='bold' class='dark:fill-slate-200'>4. Reciprocal Proportions (Richter)</text>\n        <text x='45' y='333' fill='#64748b' font-size='10' class='dark:fill-slate-400'>Fixed H in CH₄ &amp; H₂O → C:O mass ratio 3:8 matches CO₂</text>\n\n        <!-- Right Column: Gaseous Volume Laws -->\n        <rect x='410' y='70' width='370' height='295' rx='12' fill='#f8fafc' stroke='#e2e8f0' stroke-width='1.5' class='dark:fill-slate-800/50 dark:stroke-slate-700'/>\n        <rect x='420' y='80' width='350' height='28' rx='6' fill='url(#locGradGas)'/>\n        <text x='595' y='98' text-anchor='middle' fill='#ffffff' font-size='12' font-weight='bold' font-family='sans-serif'>GASEOUS VOLUME LAWS (At Same T &amp; P)</text>\n\n        <!-- Box 5: Gay-Lussac's Law -->\n        <rect x='425' y='118' width='340' height='112' rx='8' fill='#ffffff' stroke='#cbd5e1' class='dark:fill-slate-800 dark:stroke-slate-600'/>\n        <text x='435' y='138' fill='#1e293b' font-size='11' font-weight='bold' class='dark:fill-slate-200'>5. Gay-Lussac's Gas Volumes (1808)</text>\n        <text x='435' y='156' fill='#64748b' font-size='10' class='dark:fill-slate-400'>Reacting gas volumes bear simple whole-number ratios.</text>\n        <text x='435' y='174' fill='#047857' font-size='10' font-weight='bold' class='dark:fill-emerald-400'>Example: H₂(g) + Cl₂(g) → 2HCl(g)</text>\n        <text x='435' y='192' fill='#64748b' font-size='10' class='dark:fill-slate-400'>1 vol H₂  +  1 vol Cl₂  →  2 vol HCl  (Ratio 1 : 1 : 2)</text>\n        <text x='435' y='210' fill='#dc2626' font-size='9' font-weight='bold'>Note: Applies ONLY to gases under identical T and P!</text>\n\n        <!-- Box 6: Avogadro's Law -->\n        <rect x='425' y='242' width='340' height='108' rx='8' fill='#ffffff' stroke='#cbd5e1' class='dark:fill-slate-800 dark:stroke-slate-600'/>\n        <text x='435' y='262' fill='#1e293b' font-size='11' font-weight='bold' class='dark:fill-slate-200'>6. Avogadro's Law (1811)</text>\n        <text x='435' y='280' fill='#64748b' font-size='10' class='dark:fill-slate-400'>Equal volumes of ALL gases at same T &amp; P contain</text>\n        <text x='435' y='298' fill='#64748b' font-size='10' class='dark:fill-slate-400'>equal numbers of molecules (V ∝ n).</text>\n        <text x='435' y='318' fill='#2563eb' font-size='10' font-weight='bold' class='dark:fill-blue-400'>Key: V₁/n₁ = V₂/n₂  →  Resolves diatomic molecules!</text>\n      </svg>"
    },
    "neetImportantPoints": [
      "Conservation of mass applies strictly to closed chemical systems; mass of reactants consumed equals mass of products formed.",
      "Law of Definite Proportions applies strictly to pure chemical compounds, NOT to variable-composition mixtures.",
      "In Law of Multiple Proportions, the mass of ONE element must be kept constant before taking the mass ratio of the second element.",
      "Multiple Proportions ratio must yield small whole numbers (e.g. 1:2, 2:3, 1:3).",
      "Reciprocal Proportions compares three elements forming three separate binary compounds.",
      "Gay-Lussac's Law applies ONLY to gaseous reactants and products under identical temperature and pressure.",
      "Avogadro's Law establishes that equal volumes of gases at constant T and P contain equal numbers of molecules (V ∝ n).",
      "Do not confuse Avogadro's Law (V ∝ n) with molar volume at STP (22.4 L/mol).",
      "These empirical laws historically provided the quantitative foundation for Dalton's Atomic Theory."
    ],
