        "paragraphs": [
          "To calculate the empirical formula from elemental mass percentages or elemental masses, follow this rigorous 6-step algorithm:",
          "• Step 1: Assume a total sample mass of 100 grams (if data is given as percentages). Then the mass percentage of each element directly equals its mass in grams.",
          "• Step 2: Record the mass (in grams) for each constituent element present in the compound.",
          "• Step 3: Convert the mass of each element into moles of atoms using the fundamental formula:nMoles of atoms = (Given Mass of Element in g) / (Gram Atomic Mass of Element)",
          "• Step 4: Divide every mole value obtained in Step 3 by the smallest mole value among all elements to determine the relative atomic ratio.",
          "• Step 5: Convert the relative atomic ratios into the simplest whole-number ratio. If any ratio ends in a fraction (e.g. 1.5 or 1.33), multiply ALL ratios by the appropriate integer factor (2, 3, or 4).",
          "• Step 6: Write the empirical formula by placing the whole-number ratios as subscripts next to their respective elemental symbols."
        ]
