      "2. Divide all mole values by the SMALLEST mole value.",
      "3. If ratios are fractional (e.g. 1.5 or 1.33), multiply ALL by 2 or 3 to get whole numbers.",
      "4. Write Empirical Formula using these whole-number subscripts.",
      "5. Calculate Empirical Formula Mass (EFM).",
      "6. Find multiplier n = Molecular Molar Mass / EFM (or Molar Mass = 2 × Vapor Density).",
