      "2. Convert given quantity to moles (n = m/M).",
      "3. For multiple reactants, find Limiting Reagent by comparing (n_given / ν).",
      "4. Use coefficient ratio from LR: Moles Target = Moles LR × (ν_Target / ν_LR).",
      "5. Convert target moles to requested unit (Mass = n × M, Vol = n × 22.4 L).",
      "6. Calculate Excess Remaining = Initial Moles - Consumed Moles.",
      "7. Calculate % Yield = (Actual Yield / Theoretical Yield) × 100.",
      "8. Calculate Pure Mass = Impure Sample Mass × (% Purity / 100)."
