        "heading": "11. Isotopes, Isobars, Isotones & Related Species",
        "paragraphs": [
          "• Isotopes: Same Z, different A. Examples: Protium (¹₁H), Deuterium (²₁H), Tritium (³₁H); Carbon-12 (¹²₆C) and Carbon-14 (¹⁴₆C); Chlorine-35 (³⁵₁₇Cl) and Chlorine-37 (³⁷₁₇Cl). Identical chemical properties, different physical properties.",
          "• Isobars: Same A, different Z. Examples: ⁴⁰₁₈Ar, ⁴⁰₁₉K, ⁴⁰₂₀Ca. Different elements, completely different chemical properties.",
          "• Isotones: Same number of neutrons N = A − Z. Examples: ¹⁴₆C (N=8) and ¹⁶₈O (N=8); ³⁰₁₄Si, ³¹₁₅P, ³²₁₆S (all N=16).",
          "• Isoelectronic Species: Same total electron count. Examples: N³⁻, O²⁻, F⁻, Ne, Na⁺, Mg²⁺, Al³⁺ (all have 10 electrons). Ionic radius DECREASES as nuclear charge Z increases for isoelectronic ions!"
        ]
