          "  - Bond breaking requires energy ➔ ENDOTHERMIC (+ve contribution).",
          "  - Bond formation releases energy ➔ EXOTHERMIC (−ve contribution).",
          "• Mean (Average) Bond Enthalpy: In polyatomic molecules (like CH₄), the four C−H bonds do not require identical energy to break sequentially. The average value across all four steps is taken as the mean bond enthalpy (e.g., C−H bond enthalpy in CH₄ = 416 kJ mol⁻¹).",
          "• Calculating Reaction Enthalpy from Bond Enthalpies:",
          "  Δ_r H° ≈ Σ [Bond Enthalpies of Bonds BROKEN in Reactants] − Σ [Bond Enthalpies of Bonds FORMED in Products]",
          "  Δ_r H° = Σ B.E.(reactants) − Σ B.E.(products)",
