        "formula": "V = I \\cdot R",
        "meaning": "The electric potential difference across a linear conductor is directly proportional to the current flowing through it at constant physical conditions.",
        "symbols": "V = potential difference across conductor (V), I = electric current (A), R = electrical resistance (Ω).",
